srow(174, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THESE NATIONS WHICH YOU DISPOSSESS" (18:14) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE MATTER, FOR BY ITS REWARD YOU DISPOSSESS THESE NATIONS. The head row of piska 174 ({SP_(174, 1, "שבשכרה", "אתה", "יורש", "את", "הגוים", "האלה")} "for by its reward you dispossess these nations"): the entry formula\'s fourth seat — the dispossession the bar\'s reward (9:5\'s "for the wickedness of these nations" the kin, five tokens shared, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(174, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO SOOTHSAYERS AND TO DIVINERS THEY HEARKEN" — LEST YOU SAY: THEY HAVE SOMETHING TO ASK AND I HAVE NOT? "BUT YOU — NOT SO: THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS GIVEN YOU". "GIVEN YOU" — TO YOU IT WAS GIVEN, AND YOU LEAVE THE WORDS OF TORAH AND BUSY YOURSELF WITH ITS NULLIFYING? ({SP_(174, 2, "להם", "יש", "במה", "להשאל", "ולי", "אין", "לי")} "they have something to ask and I have not"; {SP_(174, 2, "לך", "נתנה")} "to you it was given"): THE TORAH THE ORACLE ISRAEL HAS — "not so has the LORD your God given you" read as the given thing (the English\'s note: an insertion out of sequence): the nations\' oracles against the given Torah — the compile\'s Israel asks the Torah\'s daemon, not the diviners\'; 18:15\'s prophet the next verse\'s answer. Fresh.')
srow(175, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"A PROPHET FROM YOUR MIDST" (18:15) — AND NOT FROM OUTSIDE THE LAND; "OF YOUR BROTHERS" — NOT FROM OTHERS; "THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL RAISE UP FOR YOU" — NOT FOR THE NATIONS. THEN HOW "A PROPHET TO THE NATIONS I MADE YOU" (JEREMIAH 1:5)? ONE WHO BEHAVES LIKE THE NATIONS. The head row of piska 175 ({SP_(175, 1, "ולא", "מחוצה", "לארץ")} "and not from outside the land"; {SP_(175, 1, "ולא", "לגוים")} "and not for the nations"; {SP_(175, 1, "בנוהג", "מנהג", "גוים")} "one who behaves in the nations\' way"): THE PROPHET\'S THREE CONDITIONS THE KING\'S (157:4-5\'s "from among, your brothers" — the same two words, the same two exclusions; "a prophet from your midst like me" one seat, asserted) — and Jeremiah\'s commission resolved: the compile\'s prophet daemon\'s subject an Israelite of the land, its audience Israel. Fresh.')
srow(175, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO HIM YOU SHALL HEARKEN" — EVEN IF HE TELLS YOU TO TRANSGRESS ONE OF THE COMMANDMENTS SAID IN THE TORAH, LIKE ELIJAH ON MOUNT CARMEL — FOR THE HOUR — OBEY HIM. ({SP_(175, 2, "עבר", "על", "אחת", "מן", "המצוות")} "transgress one of the commandments"; {SP_(175, 2, "לפי", "שעה", "שמע", "לו")} "for the hour — obey him"): THE PROPHET OVERRIDES A COMMANDMENT FOR THE HOUR (Elijah\'s altar outside the place — 1 Kings 18 the run\'s case; Yevamot 90b the segment if a cell needs it): "you (pl.) shall hearken" (the verse\'s one plural, asserted); ONKELOS "you shall accept": the compile\'s prophet effect a temporary override of the place\'s bar — a parameter with a duration. Fresh.')
