srow(178, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF YOU SAY, HOW SHALL WE KNOW THE WORD" (18:21) — YOU WILL SAY IT: JEREMIAH SAID "THE VESSELS OF THE HOUSE GO TO BABYLON" (27:22) AND HANANIAH "THE VESSELS RETURN FROM BABYLON" (27:16) — WHOM SHALL I HEED? THE TEACHING SAYS (18:22) "WHAT THE PROPHET SPEAKS IN THE LORD\'S NAME AND IT IS NOT AND COMES NOT, THAT IS THE WORD THE LORD HAS NOT SPOKEN". WHICH WORD DID THE PLACE SPEAK? THE ONE HE SAYS AND IT COMES. "PRESUMPTUOUSLY THE PROPHET SPOKE IT" — FOR PRESUMPTION HE IS LIABLE, NOT FOR ERROR. ({SP_(178, 2, "עתידים", "אתם", "לומר", "איכה", "נדע", "הדבר")} "you will one day say, how shall we know the word"; {SP_(178, 2, "ואיני", "יודע", "למי", "אשמע")} "and I do not know whom to heed"; {SP_(178, 2, "זה", "שאומר", "ובא")} "the one he says and it comes"): THE TEST OF THE WORD BY ITS COMING — Jeremiah against Hananiah the run\'s case (18:22 shares three tokens with Jeremiah 28:9, asserted): A LAW WHOSE VERDICT WAITS ON THE TAPE\'S FUTURE — the prophet\'s word graded when its event arrives (the readback\'s question, THE_LOOP step 6); "presumptuously" 155:3\'s condition again (the noun\'s two Torah seats, asserted): the compile\'s prophet cell a deferred verdict with an intent condition. Fresh.')
